","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Our company''s new product is receiving a good reputation in the market.","jp":"当社の新製品は市場で好評を得ています。"}},{"english":"text / writing / sentence","reading":"ぶんしょう","japanese":"文章","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"His writing is easy to read.","jp":"彼の文章は読みやすい。"}},{"english":"prohibition / ban / forbidden","reading":"きんし","japanese":"禁止","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"No entry. / Entry prohibited.","jp":"立ち入り禁止。"}},{"english":"protect / shield / defend","reading":"かばう","japanese":"かばう","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He covered for his friend''s mistake.","jp":"彼は友達の失敗をかばった。"}},{"english":"discussion / talk / consultation","reading":"はなしあい","japanese":"話し合い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We had a discussion about our future plans.","jp":"私たちは今後の計画について話し合いをしました。"}},{"english":"swallow / gulp down / engulf","reading":"のみこむ","japanese":"飲み込む","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The pill was too big, so it was hard to swallow.","jp":"薬が大きすぎて、飲み込むのが大変だった。"}},{"english":"wipe / dry / clear away","reading":"ぬぐう","japanese":"拭う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"She wiped the sweat with a handkerchief.","jp":"彼女はハンカチで汗を拭った。"}},{"english":"express / represent / show","reading":"あらわす","japanese":"表す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He expressed his gratitude.","jp":"彼は感謝の気持ちを表した。"}},{"english":"go / receive / pick up","reading":"うけとってくる","japanese":"受け取ってくる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''ll go pick up the package at the post office and come back.","jp":"郵便局で荷物を受け取ってくる。"}},{"english":"badmouthing / insult / slander","reading":"わるくち","japanese":"悪口","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He''s always badmouthing other people.","jp":"彼はいつも人の悪口ばかり言っている。"}},{"english":"preservation / conservation / storage","reading":"ほぞん","japanese":"保存","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please be sure to save this file.","jp":"このファイルは必ず保存してください。"}},{"english":"welcome / reception","reading":"かんげい","japanese":"歓迎","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Thank you for your heartfelt welcome.","jp":"心からの歓迎をありがとうございます。"}},{"english":"wake up / awaken / sober up","reading":"さめる","japanese":"覚める","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I woke up from my sleep due to a sudden noise.","jp":"突然の物音で眠りから覚めた。"}},{"english":"lines / dialogue / speech","reading":"セリフ","japanese":"セリフ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This actor always remembers their lines perfectly.","jp":"この役者はいつもセリフを完璧に覚えている。"}},{"english":"results / record / performance","reading":"せいせき","japanese":"成績","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He achieved good grades at school.","jp":"彼は学校で良い成績を収めた。"}},{"english":"cancellation / suspension","reading":"ちゅうし","japanese":"中止","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The event was cancelled.","jp":"イベントは中止になりました。"}},{"english":"assemble / put together","reading":"くみたてる","japanese":"組み立てる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This furniture needs to be assembled by yourself.","jp":"この家具は自分で組み立てる必要があります。"}},{"english":"workplace / office / job site","reading":"しょくば","japanese":"職場","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Human relationships at the workplace are important.","jp":"職場での人間関係は重要です。"}},{"english":"face / head towards","reading":"むかう","japanese":"向かう","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"We are heading towards the station.","jp":"私たちは駅に向かっています。"}},{"english":"apply for / subscribe","reading":"もうしこむ","japanese":"申し込む","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To apply for participation in the seminar.","jp":"セミナーへの参加を申し込む。"}},{"english":"cause / origin / source","reading":"げんいん","japanese":"原因","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We are investigating the cause of the accident.","jp":"事故の原因を調査しています。"}},{"english":"finish / end / complete","reading":"しゅうりょうする","japanese":"終了する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The meeting will finish at 5 PM.","jp":"会議は午後5時に終了します。"}},{"english":"report","reading":"ほうこくする","japanese":"報告する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To report progress at the meeting.","jp":"会議で進捗を報告する。"}},{"english":"resemble / be similar","reading":"にる","japanese":"似る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He resembles his father very much.","jp":"彼は父親にとても似ている。"}},{"english":"light / lamp / gleam","reading":"あかり","japanese":"明かり","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The room is dark, so please turn on the light.","jp":"部屋が暗いので、明かりをつけてください。"}},{"english":"cooperate / collaborate","reading":"きょうりょくする","japanese":"協力する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"We all cooperated and made the project a success.","jp":"みんなで協力してプロジェクトを成功させた。"}},{"english":"shake / sway / tremble","reading":"ゆれる","japanese":"揺れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The building shook violently in the earthquake.","jp":"地震で建物が大きく揺れた。"}},{"english":"take out / pull out","reading":"とりだす","japanese":"取り出す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To take out a wallet from a bag.","jp":"カバンから財布を取り出す。"}},{"english":"subway / underground train","reading":"ちかてつ","japanese":"地下鉄","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I commute by subway every day.","jp":"毎日地下鉄で通勤しています。"}},{"english":"production / manufacture","reading":"せいさん","japanese":"生産","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This factory produces cars.","jp":"この工場は車を生産しています。"}},{"english":"notebook / pocket diary","reading":"てちょう","japanese":"手帳","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Write down the schedule in a notebook.","jp":"予定を手帳に書く。"}},{"english":"action / conduct / behavior","reading":"こうどう","japanese":"行動","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"His actions are incomprehensible.","jp":"彼の行動は理解できない。"}},{"english":"handshake","reading":"あくしゅ","japanese":"握手","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I shook hands with him.","jp":"彼と握手した。"}},{"english":"rooftop","reading":"おくじょう","japanese":"屋上","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Let''s eat lunch on the rooftop.","jp":"屋上でランチを食べましょう。"}},{"english":"limbs / hands / feet","reading":"てあし","japanese":"手足","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"My hands and feet are cold from the cold.","jp":"寒くて手足が冷たい。"}},{"english":"magic trick / sleight of hand","reading":"てじな","japanese":"手品","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He is good at magic tricks.","jp":"彼は手品が得意だ。"}},{"english":"circumstances / conditions / reasons","reading":"じじょう","japanese":"事情","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I was late due to various circumstances.","jp":"色々な事情があって遅れました。"}},{"english":"roughly","reading":"だいたい","japanese":"だいたい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I understand roughly.","jp":"だいたいわかりました。"}},{"english":"sample / model / specimen","reading":"みほん","japanese":"見本","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Look at a sample of the new product.","jp":"新製品の見本を見る。"}},{"english":"convention / tournament / mass meeting","reading":"たいかい","japanese":"大会","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Participate in a sports tournament.","jp":"スポーツ大会に参加する。"}},{"english":"snack / eating between meals","reading":"かんしょく","japanese":"間食","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''m refraining from snacking for my health.","jp":"健康のために間食を控えている。"}},{"english":"grumbling / nagging / scolding repeatedly","reading":"ガミガミ","japanese":"ガミガミ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The teacher always scolds the students who forget their homework.","jp":"先生はいつも宿題を忘れる生徒にガミガミ言う。"}},{"english":"condition / term / requirement","reading":"じょうけん","japanese":"条件","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There are several **conditions** for this contract.","jp":"この契約にはいくつかの**条件**があります。"}},{"english":"draft / rough copy / outline","reading":"したがき","japanese":"下書き","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''ve just finished writing the draft of the report.","jp":"レポートの下書きを書き終えたばかりだ。"}},{"english":"record / document / minutes","reading":"きろく","japanese":"記録","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He broke the world record.","jp":"彼は世界記録を更新した。"}},{"english":"religion","reading":"しゅうきょう","japanese":"宗教","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Many different religions exist in the world.","jp":"世界には多くの異なる宗教が存在する。"}},{"english":"faith / belief / creed","reading":"しんこう","japanese":"信仰","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He has deep faith in God.","jp":"彼は神への信仰心が厚い。"}},{"english":"be silent / shut up / keep quiet","reading":"だまる","japanese":"黙る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He remained silent even when questioned.","jp":"彼は質問されても黙っていた。"}},{"english":"number of years","reading":"ねんすう","japanese":"年数","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"His **number of years** at this company is 10.","jp":"彼のこの会社での**年数**は10年です。"}},{"english":"victory / triumph","reading":"しょうり","japanese":"勝利","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"After a tough battle, the team achieved victory.","jp":"チームは厳しい戦いの末、勝利を収めた。"}},{"english":"be scolded / get a scolding","reading":"しかられる","japanese":"叱られる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He was scolded by the teacher and is feeling down.","jp":"彼は先生に叱られて、落ち込んでいる。"}},{"english":"be in time for / make it in time / be on time","reading":"まにあう","japanese":"間に合う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I hurried so that I would make it in time for the train.","jp":"電車に間に合うように急いだ。"}},{"english":"disappointed / dejected / disheartened","reading":"がっかり","japanese":"がっかり","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I was disappointed that I failed the exam.","jp":"試験に落ちてがっかりした。"}},{"english":"refrigerator / fridge","reading":"れいぞうこ","japanese":"冷蔵庫","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There is milk in the refrigerator.","jp":"冷蔵庫に牛乳があります。"}},{"english":"you","reading":"きみ","japanese":"君","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"pronoun","exampleSentence":{"en":"What are you thinking?","jp":"君は何を考えているの？"}},{"english":"sweet / naive / lenient","reading":"あまい","japanese":"甘い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This cake is very sweet.","jp":"このケーキはとても甘い。"}},{"english":"isn''t it? / wow / hey","reading":"なあ","japanese":"なあ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"particle","exampleSentence":{"en":"What nice weather, isn''t it!","jp":"いい天気だなあ。"}},{"english":";;","reading":"って","japanese":"って","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"particle","exampleSentence":{"en":"Could you buy it and bring it back?","jp":"買ってきてくれる？"}},{"english":"second","reading":"びょう","japanese":"秒","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There are five seconds left.","jp":"あと五秒です。"}},{"english":"immediately / right away / soon","reading":"すぐに","japanese":"直ぐに","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please come right away.","jp":"直ぐに来てください。"}},{"english":"probably / perhaps","reading":"たぶん","japanese":"多分","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"It will probably rain.","jp":"多分、雨が降るでしょう。"}},{"english":"surely / certainly","reading":"きっと","japanese":"きっと","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"It will surely be fine.","jp":"きっと大丈夫です。"}},{"english":"of course","reading":"もちろん","japanese":"もちろん","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Of course, I will help.","jp":"もちろん、手伝いますよ。"}},{"english":"entrance","reading":"いりぐち","japanese":"入口","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The entrance is over there.","jp":"入口はあちらです。"}},{"english":"exit","reading":"でぐち","japanese":"出口","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Where is the exit?","jp":"出口はどこですか？"}},{"english":"onion","reading":"たまねぎ","japanese":"玉ねぎ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''ll sauté the onions to make curry.","jp":"カレーを作るために、玉ねぎを炒めます。"}},{"english":"look! / hey! / see!","reading":"ほら","japanese":"ほら","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"Look, there''s a cat over there.","jp":"ほら、あそこに猫がいるよ。"}},{"english":"until now / up to now / so far","reading":"いままで","japanese":"いままで","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Thank you for everything until now.","jp":"今までありがとう。"}},{"english":"can do","reading":"できる","japanese":"できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can speak Japanese.","jp":"私は日本語ができます。"}},{"english":"want to","reading":"いたい","japanese":"いたい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to watch a movie.","jp":"映画を見たい。"}},{"english":"how many / how old","reading":"いくつ","japanese":"幾つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"How many apples are there?","jp":"りんごが幾つありますか？"}},{"english":"how much","reading":"いくら","japanese":"幾ら","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"How much is this T-shirt?","jp":"このTシャツは幾らですか？"}},{"english":"how / in what way","reading":"どう","japanese":"どう","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"How are you doing?","jp":"調子はどうですか？"}},{"english":"therefore / so / that''s why","reading":"だから","japanese":"だから","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"conjunction","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''m busy. Therefore, I can''t go.","jp":"忙しい。だから、行けない。"}},{"english":"but / however","reading":"でも","japanese":"でも","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"conjunction","exampleSentence":{"en":"He studied hard. But, he failed the exam.","jp":"彼は一生懸命勉強した。でも、試験に落ちた。"}},{"english":"separate / different","reading":"べつ","japanese":"別","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"Let''s meet on a different day.","jp":"別の日に会いましょう。"}},{"english":"easy / simple","reading":"かんたん","japanese":"簡単","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This problem is easy.","jp":"この問題は簡単です。"}},{"english":"painful / hurt","reading":"いたい","japanese":"痛い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"My head hurts.","jp":"頭が痛いです。"}},{"english":"cold","reading":"つめたい","japanese":"冷たい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to drink cold water.","jp":"冷たい水が飲みたい。"}},{"english":"many / numerous / a lot","reading":"おおい","japanese":"多い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"There are many people here.","jp":"ここには人が多いです。"}},{"english":"few / little","reading":"すくない","japanese":"少ない","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"I have little money.","jp":"お金が少ないです。"}},{"english":"ouch! / pain","reading":"いた","japanese":"痛","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"I fell and cried out, \"Ouch!\"","jp":"転んで「痛っ！」と叫んだ。"}},{"english":"hurry / rush","reading":"いそぐ","japanese":"急ぐ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please hurry.","jp":"急いでください。"}},{"english":"send / escort / see off","reading":"おくる","japanese":"送る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To send a letter.","jp":"手紙を送る。"}},{"english":"pull / draw / subtract","reading":"ひく","japanese":"引く","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To pull the door.","jp":"ドアを引く。"}},{"english":"push / press","reading":"おす","japanese":"押す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To press a button.","jp":"ボタンを押す。"}},{"english":"get tired / be exhausted","reading":"つかれる","japanese":"疲れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To get tired from work.","jp":"仕事で疲れる。"}},{"english":"answer / solution","reading":"こたえ","japanese":"答え","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He knew the correct answer.","jp":"彼は正しい答えを知っていた。"}},{"english":"question","reading":"しつもん","japanese":"質問","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To ask the teacher a question.","jp":"先生に質問する。"}},{"english":"reply / answer","reading":"へんじ","japanese":"返事","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To write a reply to a letter.","jp":"手紙に返事を書く。"}},{"english":"promise / appointment","reading":"やくそく","japanese":"約束","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To make a promise with a friend.","jp":"友達と約束をする。"}},{"english":"plan / schedule / expectation","reading":"よてい","japanese":"予定","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"What are your plans for today?","jp":"今日の予定は何ですか。"}},{"english":"problem / question","reading":"もんだい","japanese":"問題","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A difficult problem/question.","jp":"難しい問題。"}},{"english":"exam / test","reading":"しけん","japanese":"試験","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To take an exam.","jp":"試験を受ける。"}},{"english":"example / instance","reading":"れい","japanese":"例","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"For example.","jp":"例えば。"}},{"english":"beginning / start","reading":"はじめ","japanese":"初め","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The beginning of things.","jp":"物事の初め。"}},{"english":"center / middle","reading":"まんなか","japanese":"真ん中","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The center of the room.","jp":"部屋の真ん中。"}},{"english":"all / whole / entire","reading":"ぜんぶ","japanese":"全部","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To eat everything.","jp":"全部食べる。"}},{"english":"part / section / portion","reading":"ぶぶん","japanese":"部分","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A part of the body.","jp":"体の一部。"}},{"english":"one / one item","reading":"ひとつ","japanese":"一つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please give me one apple.","jp":"りんごを一つください。"}},{"english":"two / two items","reading":"ふたつ","japanese":"二つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To buy two oranges.","jp":"みかんを二つ買う。"}},{"english":"three / three items","reading":"みっつ","japanese":"三つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To eat three cakes.","jp":"ケーキを三つ食べる。"}},{"english":"four / four items","reading":"よっつ","japanese":"四つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There are four boxes.","jp":"箱が四つある。"}},{"english":"five / five items","reading":"いつつ","japanese":"五つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"To hold five pencils.","jp":"鉛筆を五つ持つ。"}},{"english":"six / six items","reading":"むっつ","japanese":"六つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Six eggs.","jp":"六つの卵。"}},{"english":"seven / seven items","reading":"ななつ","japanese":"七つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Seven colors.","jp":"七つの色。"}},{"english":"eight / eight items","reading":"やっつ","japanese":"八つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Eight stars.","jp":"八つの星。"}},{"english":"nine / nine items","reading":"ここのつ","japanese":"九つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Nine balls.","jp":"九つのボール。"}},{"english":"if / when","reading":"たら","japanese":"たら","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"particle","exampleSentence":{"en":"**If** it rains, the excursion will be canceled.","jp":"もし雨が降っ**たら**、遠足は中止になります。"}},{"english":"role / duty / use","reading":"やく","japanese":"役","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"His role is important.","jp":"彼の役は重要だ。"}},{"english":"region / district / area","reading":"ちほう","japanese":"地方","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He got a job not in Tokyo, but in the provinces (or a regional area).","jp":"彼は東京ではなく、地方で就職しました。"}},{"english":"access / connection","reading":"せつぞく","japanese":"接続","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Internet access (connection) has been restored.","jp":"インターネットへの接続が回復しました。"}},{"english":"access / connect","reading":"せつぞくする","japanese":"接続する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you access this website?","jp":"このウェブサイトにアクセスできますか？"}},{"english":"surely / certainly / without fail","reading":"かならず","japanese":"必ず","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He will surely come.","jp":"彼は必ず来るだろう。"}},{"english":"especially / particularly / in particular","reading":"とくに","japanese":"特に","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Among fruits, I especially like apples.","jp":"私は果物の中でも特にりんごが好きです。"}},{"english":"straight / directly","reading":"まっすぐ","japanese":"真っ直ぐ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please go straight down this road.","jp":"この道を真っ直ぐ行ってください。"}},{"english":"reservation / booking / appointment","reading":"よやく","japanese":"予約","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''d like to make a reservation.","jp":"予約をお願いします。"}},{"english":"order","reading":"ちゅうもん","japanese":"注文","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"May I order?","jp":"注文してもいいですか？"}},{"english":"cash","reading":"げんきん","japanese":"現金","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please pay with cash.","jp":"お支払いは現金でお願いします。"}},{"english":"bag / sack / pouch","reading":"ふくろ","japanese":"袋","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Do you need a bag?","jp":"袋は必要ですか？"}},{"english":"change","reading":"おつり","japanese":"お釣り","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Keep the change.","jp":"お釣りは結構です。"}},{"english":"pharmacy / drugstore","reading":"やっきょく","japanese":"薬局","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Where is the pharmacy?","jp":"薬局はどこにありますか？"}},{"english":"souvenir / gift","reading":"おみやげ","japanese":"お土産","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This is a souvenir/gift.","jp":"これはお土産です。"}},{"english":"police","reading":"けいさつ","japanese":"警察","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"If you get lost, ask the police.","jp":"道に迷ったら、警察に聞きましょう。"}},{"english":"last time / previous time / previous occasion","reading":"ぜんかい","japanese":"前回","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The last meeting was cancelled.","jp":"前回の会議は中止になりました。"}},{"english":"swimsuit / bathing suit","reading":"みずぎ","japanese":"水着","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I bought a new swimsuit for the summer.","jp":"夏に向けて新しい水着を買った。"}},{"english":"sunrise","reading":"ひので","japanese":"日の出","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We woke up early to see the beautiful sunrise.","jp":"私たちは美しい日の出を見るために早起きしました。"}},{"english":"center / core / focus","reading":"ちゅうしん","japanese":"中心","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The station is the center of this town.","jp":"この街は駅が中心です。"}},{"english":"added","reading":"たした","japanese":"足した","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I like coffee with sugar added.","jp":"砂糖を足したコーヒーが好きです。"}},{"english":"increased / multiplied","reading":"ふやした","japanese":"増やした","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He increased the company''s profit.","jp":"彼は会社の利益を増やした。"}},{"english":"failure / mistake / blunder","reading":"しっぱい","japanese":"失敗","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The first attempt was a failure.","jp":"最初の試みは失敗だった。"}},{"english":"tablespoon","reading":"おおさじ","japanese":"大さじ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please add one tablespoon of sugar.","jp":"砂糖を大さじ一杯加えてください。"}},{"english":"thermometer","reading":"おんどけい","japanese":"温度計","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Measure the fever with a thermometer.","jp":"温度計で熱を測る。"}},{"english":"shelf / rack","reading":"たな","japanese":"棚","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I arranged the books on the shelf.","jp":"本を棚に並べた。"}},{"english":"wise / clever / intelligent","reading":"かしこい","japanese":"賢い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"She is a very clever student.","jp":"彼女はとても賢い学生だ。"}},{"english":"folding / foldable","reading":"おりたたみ","japanese":"折りたたみ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This chair is a folding type.","jp":"この椅子は折りたたみ式です。"}},{"english":"tattered / worn out / crumbling","reading":"ボロボロ","japanese":"ボロボロ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"He was wearing tattered clothes.","jp":"彼はボロボロの服を着ていた。"}},{"english":"large serving / extra-large portion","reading":"おおもり","japanese":"大盛り","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''d like a large serving of ramen, please.","jp":"ラーメンを大盛りでお願いします。"}},{"english":"yakisoba","reading":"やきそば","japanese":"焼そば","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I ate yakisoba at a festival stall.","jp":"祭りの屋台で焼そばを食べた。"}},{"english":"piggyback ride","reading":"おんぶ","japanese":"おんぶ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I carried my tired child home on my back.","jp":"疲れた子供をおんぶして家まで帰った。"}},{"english":"commute / attend / frequent","reading":"かよう","japanese":"通う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I commute to work by train every day.","jp":"毎日電車で会社に通っている。"}},{"english":"nightmare","reading":"あくむ","japanese":"悪夢","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Last night, I had a terrible nightmare.","jp":"昨夜、恐ろしい悪夢を見た。"}},{"english":"population","reading":"じんこう","japanese":"人口","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Japan''s population is on a declining trend.","jp":"日本の人口は減少傾向にある。"}},{"english":"is living / is alive / be alive","reading":"いきている","japanese":"生きている","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I believe he is still alive.","jp":"彼はまだ生きていると信じている。"}},{"english":"textbook","reading":"きょうかしょ","japanese":"教科書","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This textbook is used in university classes.","jp":"この教科書は、大学の授業で使われています。"}},{"english":"fire / conflagration","reading":"かじ","japanese":"火事","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A fire broke out in the house next door.","jp":"隣の家で火事が起きた。"}},{"english":"market","reading":"しじょう","japanese":"市場","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We analyze global market trends.","jp":"世界の市場動向を分析する。"}},{"english":"information / data","reading":"じょうほう","japanese":"情報","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I obtained the latest information.","jp":"最新の情報を入手しました。"}},{"english":"powder / flour / dust","reading":"こな","japanese":"粉","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There was white powder on the table.","jp":"テーブルの上に白い粉が落ちていた。"}},{"english":"fee / charge / fare","reading":"りょうきん","japanese":"料金","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The fee for this parking lot is expensive.","jp":"この駐車場の料金は高いです。"}},{"english":"traffic / transportation","reading":"こうつう","japanese":"交通","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Tokyo''s traffic is always congested.","jp":"東京の交通はいつも混雑しています。"}},{"english":"accident","reading":"じこ","japanese":"事故","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There was a traffic accident in front of the station yesterday.","jp":"昨日、駅前で交通事故がありました。"}},{"english":"elephant","reading":"ぞう","japanese":"象","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"An elephant is a very large animal.","jp":"象はとても大きな動物です。"}},{"english":"dangerous / hazardous / risky","reading":"きけんな","japanese":"危険な","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"That is a very dangerous act.","jp":"それは大変危険な行為です。"}},{"english":"product / merchandise / goods","reading":"しょうひん","japanese":"商品","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This new product is selling like hotcakes.","jp":"この新しい商品は飛ぶように売れています。"}},{"english":"weekday / ordinary day","reading":"へいじつ","japanese":"平日","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I work from 9 AM to 5 PM on weekdays.","jp":"平日は朝9時から夜5時まで働いています。"}},{"english":"document / papers","reading":"しょるい","japanese":"書類","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please sign these documents.","jp":"この書類にサインしてください。"}},{"english":"conference room / meeting room","reading":"かいぎしつ","japanese":"会議室","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The meeting room is on the third floor.","jp":"会議室は3階にあります。"}},{"english":"used bookstore / second-hand bookstore","reading":"ふるほんや","japanese":"古本屋","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I found an interesting book at a used bookstore on the weekend.","jp":"週末に古本屋で面白い本を見つけました。"}},{"english":"automatic / automation","reading":"じどう","japanese":"自動","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This door opens automatically.","jp":"このドアは自動で開きます。"}},{"english":"daily life / everyday / ordinary","reading":"にちじょう","japanese":"日常","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This is a scene from my daily life.","jp":"これは私の日常の風景です。"}},{"english":"salary / pay / wages","reading":"きゅうりょう","japanese":"給料","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"When is this month''s salary?","jp":"今月の給料はいつですか？"}},{"english":"protect / defend / keep","reading":"まもる","japanese":"守る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will fight to protect my family.","jp":"家族を守るために戦う。"}},{"english":"in-store / inside the store / on the premises","reading":"てんない","japanese":"店内","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Will you eat in-store, or is it for takeout?","jp":"店内で食べますか、それとも持ち帰りですか？"}},{"english":"a second helping / another serving / refill","reading":"おかわり","japanese":"おかわり","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"You can have as many refills of rice as you like.","jp":"ご飯のおかわり自由です。"}},{"english":"machine / mechanism","reading":"きかい","japanese":"機械","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The latest machines were introduced into the factory.","jp":"工場には最新の機械が導入された。"}},{"english":"humid / hot / sultry","reading":"むしあつい","japanese":"蒸し暑い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"Today''s weather is very hot and humid.","jp":"今日の天気はとても蒸し暑い。"}},{"english":"land / plot of land / soil","reading":"とち","japanese":"土地","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He purchased a new plot of land.","jp":"彼は新しい土地を購入した。"}},{"english":"factory / plant / mill","reading":"こうじょう","japanese":"工場","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"That factory produces automobiles.","jp":"その工場では自動車を生産している。"}},{"english":"seashore / coast / beach","reading":"かいがん","japanese":"海岸","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We watched the sunset on the seashore.","jp":"私たちは海岸で夕日を見ました。"}},{"english":"polite / careful / courteous","reading":"ていねい","japanese":"丁寧","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"He always uses polite language.","jp":"彼はいつも丁寧な言葉遣いをする。"}},{"english":"break / destroy / smash","reading":"こわす","japanese":"壊す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The child broke the toy.","jp":"子供がおもちゃを壊した。"}},{"english":"calling","reading":"よんでる","japanese":"呼んでる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Someone is calling me.","jp":"誰かが私を呼んでる。"}},{"english":"voice / sound","reading":"こえ","japanese":"声","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Her voice is beautiful.","jp":"彼女の声は美しい。"}},{"english":"can hear / audible","reading":"きこえてる","japanese":"聞こえてる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can hear sounds from outside.","jp":"外の音が聞こえてる。"}},{"english":"what kind of / what sort of","reading":"どんな","japanese":"どんな","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"What kind of books do you like?","jp":"どんな本が好きですか。"}},{"english":"that day","reading":"あのひ","japanese":"あの日","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can''t forget about that day.","jp":"あの日のことは忘れられない。"}},{"english":"small / little","reading":"ちいさな","japanese":"小さな","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"A small dog ran up to me.","jp":"小さな犬が駆け寄ってきた。"}},{"english":"nowhere / anywhere","reading":"どこにも","japanese":"どこにも","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I don''t want to go anywhere.","jp":"どこにも行きたくない。"}},{"english":"all the time / for a long time / throughout","reading":"ずっと","japanese":"ずっと","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He has lived in Japan all this time.","jp":"彼はずっと日本に住んでいる。"}},{"english":"strongly / powerfully / intensely","reading":"つよく","japanese":"強く","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He gripped it strongly.","jp":"彼は強く握りしめた。"}},{"english":"no one / nobody / everyone","reading":"だれも","japanese":"誰も","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"No one came.","jp":"誰も来なかった。"}},{"english":"ahead / future / destination","reading":"さき","japanese":"先","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"What lies ahead on the road?","jp":"道の先には何があるのだろう。"}},{"english":"day off / holiday","reading":"やすみのひ","japanese":"休みの日","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"On my days off, I usually relax at home.","jp":"休みの日には、たいてい家でゆっくり過ごします。"}},{"english":"even / but / because","reading":"だって","japanese":"だって","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"particle","exampleSentence":{"en":"Even if you''re busy, there''s time to eat, you know.","jp":"忙しいだって、ご飯を食べる時間はありますよ。"}},{"english":"want to meet / want to see","reading":"あいたい","japanese":"会いたい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to meet my friends after a long time.","jp":"久しぶりに友達に会いたい。"}},{"english":"post office","reading":"ゆうびんきょく","japanese":"郵便局","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The post office is open from 9 AM.","jp":"郵便局は午前9時から開いています。"}},{"english":"good at / proficient / one''s strong point","reading":"とくい","japanese":"得意","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"She is good at drawing pictures.","jp":"彼女は絵を描くのが得意だ。"}},{"english":"personality / character / disposition","reading":"せいかく","japanese":"性格","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"She has a kind personality.","jp":"彼女は優しい性格をしています。"}},{"english":"growth / development / growing up","reading":"せいちょう","japanese":"成長","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A child''s growth is fast.","jp":"子供の成長は早い。"}},{"english":"effort / exertion / endeavor","reading":"どりょく","japanese":"努力","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Effort is necessary for success.","jp":"成功するには努力が必要です。"}},{"english":"waste / useless / futile","reading":"むだ","japanese":"無駄","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please do not waste your time.","jp":"時間を無駄にしないでください。"}},{"english":"little by little / bit by bit / gradually","reading":"ちょっとずつ","japanese":"ちょっとずつ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Let''s study little by little every day.","jp":"毎日ちょっとずつ勉強しましょう。"}},{"english":"discovery / finding","reading":"はっけん","japanese":"発見","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The discovery of the new star had a huge impact on the scientific community.","jp":"新しい星の発見は科学界に大きな衝撃を与えた。"}},{"english":"smooth","reading":"スムーず","japanese":"スムーズ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"The meeting proceeded smoothly.","jp":"会議はスムーズに進んだ。"}},{"english":"path","reading":"とおるみち","japanese":"通る道","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"That is a sure path to success.","jp":"それは、成功への確実な通る道だ。"}},{"english":"impression","reading":"かんそう","japanese":"感想","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please tell me your impressions of the movie.","jp":"映画の感想を聞かせてください。"}},{"english":"season","reading":"しーずん","japanese":"シーズン","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Will this drama be broadcast next season too?","jp":"このドラマは来シーズンも放送されますか？"}},{"english":"get lost","reading":"まよう","japanese":"迷う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I got lost and walked to the station.","jp":"道に迷って、駅まで歩いて行った。"}},{"english":"culture","reading":"ぶんか","japanese":"文化","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Japanese culture is profound, isn''t it?","jp":"日本の文化は奥深いですね。"}},{"english":"divide","reading":"わける","japanese":"分ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I divided the cake among everyone.","jp":"ケーキをみんなで分けた。"}},{"english":"order","reading":"じゅんばん","japanese":"順番","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please line up in order.","jp":"順番に並んでください。"}},{"english":"if you like","reading":"もしよかったら","japanese":"もしよかったら","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"If you like, how about having a meal together?","jp":"もしよかったら、一緒に食事でもどうですか？"}},{"english":"other than","reading":"いがい","japanese":"以外","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Everyone except me agreed.","jp":"私以外、全員賛成した。"}},{"english":"comparatively","reading":"わりと","japanese":"割と","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This movie was comparatively interesting.","jp":"この映画は割と面白かった。"}},{"english":"kind","reading":"しゅるい","japanese":"種類","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This shop has many kinds of ramen.","jp":"この店には多くの種類のラーメンがあります。"}},{"english":"noodle","reading":"めん","japanese":"麺","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Thick noodles go well with ramen.","jp":"ラーメンには太い麺がよく合います。"}},{"english":"seaweed","reading":"のり","japanese":"海苔","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Seaweed is essential for onigiri.","jp":"おにぎりに海苔は欠かせません。"}},{"english":"worry","reading":"なやむ","japanese":"悩む","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"When I think about the future, I can''t help but worry.","jp":"将来のことを考えると、つい悩んでしまう。"}},{"english":"be conveyed","reading":"つたわる","japanese":"伝わる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"His feelings were conveyed to me.","jp":"彼の気持ちが私に伝わった。"}},{"english":"genre","reading":"ジャンル","japanese":"ジャンル","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"What genre of music do you like?","jp":"好きな音楽のジャンルは何ですか？"}},{"english":"useful","reading":"やくだつ","japanese":"役立つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This tool is very useful.","jp":"この道具はとても役立つ。"}},{"english":"throw","reading":"なげる","japanese":"投げる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Throw a ball.","jp":"ボールを投げる。"}},{"english":"usually","reading":"ふだん","japanese":"普段","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I usually commute by train.","jp":"普段は電車で通勤しています。"}},{"english":"just","reading":"ちょうど","japanese":"ちょうど","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"It just started raining now.","jp":"ちょうど今、雨が降り始めました。"}},{"english":"season","reading":"じき","japanese":"時期","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This fruit is in season during the summer.","jp":"この果物は、夏が旬の時期です。"}},{"english":"experience","reading":"たいけん","japanese":"体験","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I had a valuable experience.","jp":"貴重な体験をした。"}},{"english":"wonder","reading":"ふしぎ","japanese":"不思議","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"It was a mysterious event.","jp":"それは不思議な出来事だった。"}},{"english":"price","reading":"ねだん","japanese":"値段","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"What is the price of this item?","jp":"この商品の値段はいくらですか？"}},{"english":"reach","reading":"とどく","japanese":"届く","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The package is scheduled to arrive tomorrow.","jp":"荷物が明日届く予定です。"}},{"english":"condition","reading":"ちょうし","japanese":"調子","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Lately, I haven''t been feeling well due to a slight cold.","jp":"最近、風邪気味で調子が悪い。"}},{"english":"meeting","reading":"かいぎ","japanese":"会議","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please prepare for tomorrow''s meeting.","jp":"明日の会議の準備をしてください。"}},{"english":"partner","reading":"あいて","japanese":"相手","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He served as my partner in the meeting.","jp":"彼は、会議で私の相手を務めました。"}},{"english":"rise / go up / enter","reading":"あがる","japanese":"上がる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To go up the stairs.","jp":"階段を上がる。"}},{"english":"surprisingly / unexpectedly / contrary to expectations","reading":"いがいと","japanese":"意外と","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I thought the exam would be difficult, but I surprisingly passed easily.","jp":"難しいと思っていた試験だけど、意外と簡単に合格できた。"}},{"english":"invitation","reading":"しょうたい","japanese":"招待","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I invited her to dinner.","jp":"彼女をディナーに招待しました。"}},{"english":"progress","reading":"しんぽ","japanese":"進歩","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The progress of science and technology has enriched our lives.","jp":"科学技術の進歩は私たちの生活を豊かにした。"}},{"english":"end / tip / future","reading":"すえ","japanese":"末","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A bird is perched on the tip of the tree.","jp":"木の末に鳥がとまっている。"}},{"english":"old person / elderly person / senior citizen","reading":"ろうじん","japanese":"老人","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There are priority seats for the elderly.","jp":"老人には優先席があります。"}},{"english":"get used to / become accustomed to","reading":"なれる","japanese":"慣れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''ve started to get used to the new environment.","jp":"新しい環境に慣れてきた。"}},{"english":"main store / head office","reading":"ほんてん","japanese":"本店","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The main store of that department store is in Ginza.","jp":"そのデパートの本店は銀座にある。"}},{"english":"complexion / facial expression / look","reading":"かおいろ","japanese":"顔色","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"His complexion was bad, so I became worried.","jp":"彼は顔色が悪かったので、心配になりました。"}},{"english":"if so / in that case / then","reading":"それなら","japanese":"それなら","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"conjunction","exampleSentence":{"en":"A: \"It started raining, didn''t it?\" B: \"If so, let''s use an umbrella.\"","jp":"A: 「雨が降ってきたね。」 B: 「それなら、傘をさしましょう。」"}},{"english":"why / for what reason","reading":"どうして","japanese":"どうして","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"phrase","exampleSentence":{"en":"Why were you late?","jp":"どうして遅れたのですか？"}},{"english":"different / wrong / differ","reading":"ちがう","japanese":"違う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He and I have different opinions.","jp":"彼と私は意見が違う。"}},{"english":"attach / turn on / put on","reading":"つける","japanese":"付ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"To turn on the light.","jp":"電気をつける。"}},{"english":"last / end / final","reading":"さいご","japanese":"最後","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"The end of the movie.","jp":"映画の最後。"}},{"english":"aim for / aspire to / target","reading":"めざす","japanese":"目指す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He is aiming to become a doctor.","jp":"彼は医者になることを目指している。"}},{"english":"is attached to / is included in / comes with","reading":"についてる","japanese":"についてる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This new game console comes with a special controller.","jp":"この新しいゲーム機には特別なコントローラーがについてる。"}},{"english":"courage / bravery","reading":"ゆうき","japanese":"勇気","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"He is a courageous person.","jp":"彼は勇気のある人だ。"}},{"english":"it is there / exists there","reading":"そこにある","japanese":"そこにある","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"What I''m looking for is there.","jp":"私が探しているものはそこにある。"}},{"english":"detailed / thorough / knowledgeable","reading":"くわしい","japanese":"詳しい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please give me detailed information about that matter.","jp":"その件について詳しい情報を教えてください。"}},{"english":"bother / concern / curious","reading":"きになる","japanese":"気になる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''m always curious about that person.","jp":"あの人のことがいつも気になる。"}},{"english":"be useful / be helpful","reading":"やくにたつ","japanese":"役に立つ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This information will probably be useful for work.","jp":"この情報は仕事に役に立つでしょう。"}},{"english":"take down / lower / withdraw","reading":"おろす","japanese":"下ろす","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Withdraw money at the bank.","jp":"銀行でお金をおろす。"}},{"english":"hand over / pass / give","reading":"わたす","japanese":"渡す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I handed my homework to the teacher.","jp":"先生に宿題を渡した。"}},{"english":"leaf","reading":"はっぱ","japanese":"葉","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The tree shed its leaves.","jp":"木が葉を落とした。"}},{"english":"greeting","reading":"あいさつ","japanese":"挨拶","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I greeted my neighbor in the morning.","jp":"朝、隣の人に挨拶した。"}},{"english":"give","reading":"あげる","japanese":"あげる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Give a present to a friend.","jp":"友達にプレゼントをあげる。"}},{"english":"taste","reading":"あじ","japanese":"味","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This dish has a delicious taste.","jp":"この料理は美味しい味だ。"}},{"english":"that kind of","reading":"あんな","japanese":"あんな","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will never do that kind of thing again.","jp":"あんなことは二度としない。"}},{"english":"stone","reading":"いし","japanese":"石","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"There is a big stone in the garden.","jp":"庭に大きな石がある。"}},{"english":"above","reading":"いじょう","japanese":"以上","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Those 18 years of age or older.","jp":"１８歳以上の方。"}},{"english":"reception","reading":"うけつけ","japanese":"受付","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Check in at the hotel reception.","jp":"ホテルの受付でチェックインする。"}},{"english":"lie","reading":"うそ","japanese":"嘘","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please do not lie.","jp":"嘘をつかないでください。"}},{"english":"inside","reading":"うち","japanese":"内","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Someone is inside the house.","jp":"家の中に 誰かいる。"}},{"english":"arm","reading":"うで","japanese":"腕","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"My arm hurts.","jp":"腕が 痛い。"}},{"english":"delicious","reading":"うまい","japanese":"うまい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This cake is very delicious.","jp":"この ケーキは とても うまい。"}},{"english":"driver","reading":"うんてんしゅ","japanese":"運転手","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The taxi driver is waiting.","jp":"タクシーの 運転手が 待っている。"}},{"english":"driving","reading":"うんてん","japanese":"運転","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Are you used to driving a car?","jp":"車の 運転は 慣れていますか。"}},{"english":"celebration","reading":"おいわい","japanese":"お祝い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We will have a birthday celebration.","jp":"誕生日 お祝いを します。"}},{"english":"thanks to","reading":"おかげ","japanese":"おかげ","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Thanks to everyone, we succeeded.","jp":"皆さんの おかげで 成功しました。"}},{"english":"strange","reading":"おかしい","japanese":"おかしい","jl