く","japanese":"除く","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Remove unnecessary things.","jp":"不要なものを除く。"}},{"english":"stretch","reading":"のばす","japanese":"伸ばす","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Stretch your arms.","jp":"腕を伸ばす。"}},{"english":"extend","reading":"のびる","japanese":"延びる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The road extends far away.","jp":"道が遠くまで延びている。"}},{"english":"extend","reading":"のばす","japanese":"延ばす","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Extend the meeting until the afternoon.","jp":"会議を午後まで延ばす。"}},{"english":"measure","reading":"はかる","japanese":"計る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Measure body temperature.","jp":"体温を計る。"}},{"english":"weigh","reading":"はかる","japanese":"量る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Weigh sugar.","jp":"砂糖を量る。"}},{"english":"discuss","reading":"はなしあう","japanese":"話し合う","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Discuss the problem.","jp":"問題について話し合う。"}},{"english":"contain","reading":"ふくむ","japanese":"含む","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This fruit is rich in vitamins.","jp":"この果物にはビタミンが豊富に含まれている。"}},{"english":"include","reading":"ふくめる","japanese":"含める","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Include everyone in the list.","jp":"全員をリストに含める。"}},{"english":"mix","reading":"まぜる","japanese":"混ぜる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please mix the eggs in the bowl.","jp":"ボウルに卵を混ぜてください。"}},{"english":"burn","reading":"もやす","japanese":"燃やす","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I burned the paper.","jp":"紙を燃やしてしまった。"}},{"english":"return","reading":"もどす","japanese":"戻す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please return the book to its original place.","jp":"本を元の場所に戻してください。"}},{"english":"dirty","reading":"よごす","japanese":"汚す","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please be careful not to dirty your clothes.","jp":"服を汚さないように気をつけてください。"}},{"english":"tear","reading":"やぶる","japanese":"破る","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please don''t tear the letter.","jp":"手紙を破らないでください。"}},{"english":"prize","reading":"しょうひん","japanese":"賞品","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The prize for the contest was luxurious.","jp":"コンテストの賞品は豪華でした。"}},{"english":"souvenir","reading":"みやげもの","japanese":"土産物","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I bought souvenirs from Kyoto.","jp":"京都の土産物を買いました。"}},{"english":"tourist spot","reading":"かんこうち","japanese":"観光地","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Hakone is a popular tourist spot.","jp":"箱根は人気の観光地です。"}},{"english":"tourist","reading":"かんこうきゃく","japanese":"観光客","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"It is bustling with tourists on weekends.","jp":"週末は観光客で賑わっています。"}},{"english":"tour bus","reading":"かんこうバス","japanese":"観光バス","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The tour bus has arrived.","jp":"観光バスが到着しました。"}},{"english":"day trip","reading":"ひがえりりょこう","japanese":"日帰り旅行","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I went on a day trip on the weekend.","jp":"週末に日帰り旅行に行きました。"}},{"english":"changing room","reading":"こういしつ","japanese":"更衣室","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I changed in the gym''s changing room.","jp":"ジムの更衣室で着替えました。"}},{"english":"rest area","reading":"きゅうけいじょ","japanese":"休憩所","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I was tired, so I rested in the rest area.","jp":"疲れたので、休憩所で休みました。"}},{"english":"waiting room","reading":"まちあいしつ","japanese":"待合室","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I am waiting in the hospital waiting room.","jp":"病院の待合室で待っています。"}},{"english":"do","reading":"いたします","japanese":"いたします","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will have a meeting tomorrow.","jp":"明日、会議をいたします。"}},{"english":"be surprised","reading":"おどろきます","japanese":"驚きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I was surprised by the news.","jp":"その知らせに 驚きました。"}},{"english":"dry","reading":"かわきます","japanese":"乾きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The laundry has dried.","jp":"洗濯物が 乾きました。"}},{"english":"break","reading":"こわします","japanese":"壊します","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I broke the toy.","jp":"おもちゃを 壊してしまった。"}},{"english":"choose","reading":"えらびます","japanese":"選びます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I chose one cake.","jp":"ケーキを 一つ 選びました。"}},{"english":"bloom","reading":"さきます","japanese":"咲きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The flowers bloomed beautifully.","jp":"花が きれいに 咲きました。"}},{"english":"point","reading":"さします","japanese":"指します","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The teacher pointed to the blackboard.","jp":"先生が 黒板を 指しました。"}},{"english":"fix / repair","reading":"なおします","japanese":"直します","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I repaired the broken bicycle.","jp":"壊れた自転車を 直しました。"}},{"english":"lose","reading":"なくします","japanese":"無くします","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I lost my wallet.","jp":"財布を無くしました。"}},{"english":"hand over","reading":"わたします","japanese":"渡します","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I handed the present over to my friend.","jp":"プレゼントを 友達に 渡しました。"}},{"english":"pull","reading":"ひきます","japanese":"引きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please pull the door.","jp":"ドアを 引いてください。"}},{"english":"blow","reading":"ふきます","japanese":"吹きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The wind is blowing strongly.","jp":"風が 強く 吹いています。"}},{"english":"polish / brush","reading":"みがきます","japanese":"磨きます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I brushed my teeth cleanly.","jp":"歯を きれいに 磨きました。"}},{"english":"put away / finish","reading":"しまいます","japanese":"しまいます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I put the book away on the bookshelf.","jp":"本を 本棚に しまいました。"}},{"english":"inhale / smoke","reading":"すいます","japanese":"吸います","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I smoke cigarettes.","jp":"タバコを 吸います。"}},{"english":"live / reside","reading":"すみます","japanese":"住みます","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I live in Tokyo.","jp":"東京に 住んでいます。"}},{"english":"do one''s best","reading":"がんばる","japanese":"がんばる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will do my best for the exam.","jp":"試験のために一生懸命がんばります。"}},{"english":"circle","reading":"まる","japanese":"まる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please put a circle on the correct option.","jp":"正解の選択肢にまるをつけてください。"}},{"english":"compare","reading":"くらべる","japanese":"比べる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I compare two things.","jp":"二つのものを比べます。"}},{"english":"marry","reading":"けっこんする","japanese":"結婚する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"She will marry next year.","jp":"彼女は来年結婚します。"}},{"english":"excuse oneself","reading":"しつれいする","japanese":"失礼する","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Well then, excuse me for leaving.","jp":"では、ここで失礼します。"}},{"english":"wear","reading":"かぶる","japanese":"かぶる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please wear a hat.","jp":"帽子をかぶってください。"}},{"english":"fall","reading":"たおれる","japanese":"倒れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The tree fell due to the strong wind.","jp":"強風で木が倒れた。"}},{"english":"visit","reading":"たずねる","japanese":"訪ねる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I plan to visit a friend tomorrow.","jp":"明日、友人を訪ねる予定です。"}},{"english":"lose weight","reading":"やせる","japanese":"痩せる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I lost weight by dieting.","jp":"ダイエットして痩せた。"}},{"english":"break","reading":"おれる","japanese":"折れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The pencil broke in the middle.","jp":"鉛筆が途中で折れてしまった。"}},{"english":"get dirty","reading":"よごれる","japanese":"汚れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"My clothes got dirty with mud.","jp":"服が泥で汚れてしまった。"}},{"english":"brown","reading":"ちゃいろい","japanese":"茶色い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"The cat''s fur is brown.","jp":"猫の毛は茶色いです。"}},{"english":"round","reading":"まるい","japanese":"丸い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"A ball is round.","jp":"ボールは丸いです。"}},{"english":"cool","reading":"かっこいい","japanese":"かっこいい","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"That actor is very cool.","jp":"あの俳優はとてもかっこいいです。"}},{"english":"cousin","reading":"いとこ","japanese":"従兄弟","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I met my cousin for the first time in a while.","jp":"従兄弟と久しぶりに会った。"}},{"english":"second son","reading":"じなん","japanese":"次男","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The second son is good at sports.","jp":"次男はスポーツが得意です。"}},{"english":"second daughter","reading":"じじょ","japanese":"次女","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The second daughter likes reading.","jp":"次女は読書が好きです。"}},{"english":"youngest child","reading":"すえっこ","japanese":"末っ子","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"The youngest child is a spoiled one.","jp":"末っ子は甘えん坊だ。"}},{"english":"married couple","reading":"ふうふ","japanese":"夫婦","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"That married couple gets along very well.","jp":"その夫婦はとても仲が良い。"}},{"english":"companion","reading":"なかま","japanese":"仲間","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"We are old companions.","jp":"私たちは昔からの仲間です。"}},{"english":"colleague","reading":"どうりょう","japanese":"同僚","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I had lunch with my colleagues.","jp":"同僚とランチを食べた。"}},{"english":"superior","reading":"じょうし","japanese":"上司","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I consulted with my superior.","jp":"上司に相談しました。"}},{"english":"seniors / juniors","reading":"せんぱいこうはい","japanese":"先輩後輩","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"In university, relationships between seniors and juniors are important.","jp":"大学では先輩後輩の付き合いが大切だ。"}},{"english":"neighbor","reading":"りんじん","japanese":"隣人","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I exchange greetings with my neighbor.","jp":"隣人と挨拶を交わす。"}},{"english":"stranger","reading":"みしらぬひと","japanese":"見知らぬ人","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A stranger spoke to me.","jp":"見知らぬ人から話しかけられた。"}},{"english":"stranger","reading":"たにん","japanese":"他人","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"They get along so well, it''s like they''re not strangers.","jp":"彼らは他人とは思えないほど気が合う。"}},{"english":"instead","reading":"かわりに","japanese":"代わりに","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will go instead of him.","jp":"私は彼のかわりに行きます。"}},{"english":"naturally","reading":"しぜんに","japanese":"自然に","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"When that topic came up, he naturally smiled.","jp":"その話題になると、彼は自然に笑顔になった。"}},{"english":"clearly","reading":"はっきりと","japanese":"はっきりと","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Please speak more clearly.","jp":"もっとはっきりと話してください。"}},{"english":"quite","reading":"かなり","japanese":"かなり","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This book is quite interesting.","jp":"この本はかなり面白い。"}},{"english":"somewhat","reading":"たしょう","japanese":"多少","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This room is somewhat small.","jp":"この部屋は多少狭い。"}},{"english":"small","reading":"ちょっとした","japanese":"ちょっとした","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"This is a minor problem.","jp":"これはちょっとした問題だ。"}},{"english":"just","reading":"ほんの","japanese":"ほんの","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"There was only a little left.","jp":"ほんの少ししか残っていませんでした。"}},{"english":"only","reading":"たった","japanese":"たった","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He accomplished that all by himself.","jp":"たった一人でそれを成し遂げた。"}},{"english":"just right","reading":"ちょうどよい","japanese":"ちょうど良い","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adjective","exampleSentence":{"en":"These clothes are just the right size for me.","jp":"この服は私にちょうど良いサイズです。"}},{"english":"seriously","reading":"ほんきで","japanese":"本気で","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I''m not joking, I''m saying this seriously.","jp":"冗談ではなく、本気で言っているんだ。"}},{"english":"jokingly","reading":"じょうだんで","japanese":"冗談で","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I only said it as a joke, but they believed me.","jp":"冗談で言っただけなのに、信じられた。"}},{"english":"falsely","reading":"うそで","japanese":"うそで","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"adverb","exampleSentence":{"en":"No one listens to a story built on lies.","jp":"うそで固めた話に誰も耳を貸さない。"}},{"english":"read","reading":"よめる","japanese":"読める","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you read this book in Japanese?","jp":"この本は日本語で読めますか？"}},{"english":"write","reading":"かける","japanese":"書ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to become able to write neatly.","jp":"字をきれいに書けるようになりたい。"}},{"english":"speak","reading":"はなせる","japanese":"話せる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to become able to speak English.","jp":"英語を話せるようになりたいです。"}},{"english":"hear","reading":"きける","japanese":"聞ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I couldn''t hear much of his story.","jp":"彼の話はあまり聞けなかった。"}},{"english":"drink","reading":"のめる","japanese":"飲める","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This water can be drunk as it is.","jp":"この水はそのまま飲めます。"}},{"english":"make","reading":"つくれる","japanese":"作れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can make simple dishes myself.","jp":"簡単な料理なら自分で作れます。"}},{"english":"swim","reading":"およげる","japanese":"泳げる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can swim since I was a child.","jp":"子供の頃から泳げます。"}},{"english":"run","reading":"はしれる","japanese":"走れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"He can run very fast.","jp":"彼はとても速く走れます。"}},{"english":"walk","reading":"あるける","japanese":"歩ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"You can walk around this area.","jp":"この辺りは歩いて回れます。"}},{"english":"drive","reading":"うんてんできる","japanese":"運転できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"If you have a license, you can drive a car.","jp":"免許があれば車を運転できます。"}},{"english":"cook","reading":"りょうりできる","japanese":"料理できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"She can cook various dishes.","jp":"彼女は色々な料理ができます。"}},{"english":"sing","reading":"うたえる","japanese":"歌える","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"We can all sing songs together.","jp":"みんなで歌を歌えます。"}},{"english":"dance","reading":"おどれる","japanese":"踊れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can dance to the music.","jp":"音楽に合わせて踊れます。"}},{"english":"draw","reading":"かける","japanese":"描ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I want to become able to draw pictures beautifully.","jp":"絵をきれいに描けるようになりたい。"}},{"english":"play","reading":"ひける","japanese":"弾ける","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I envy people who can play the piano.","jp":"ピアノを弾ける人は羨ましい。"}},{"english":"remember","reading":"おぼえられる","japanese":"覚えられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"It''s difficult to remember many words at once.","jp":"たくさんの単語を一度に覚えるのは難しい。"}},{"english":"divide","reading":"わけられる","japanese":"分けられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This problem can be divided into two.","jp":"この問題を二つに分けられます。"}},{"english":"choose","reading":"えらべる","japanese":"選べる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"You can choose what you like yourself.","jp":"自分で好きなものを選べます。"}},{"english":"fix","reading":"なおせる","japanese":"直せる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you fix the broken watch?","jp":"壊れた時計を直せますか？"}},{"english":"stop","reading":"とめられる","japanese":"止められる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I was prevented from letting him out of the room.","jp":"彼を部屋から出さないように止められた。"}},{"english":"start","reading":"はじめられる","japanese":"始められる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The meeting can be started now.","jp":"会議はもう始められます。"}},{"english":"finish","reading":"おえられる","japanese":"終えられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Today''s work can be finished within the time.","jp":"今日の仕事は時間内に終えられます。"}},{"english":"open","reading":"あけられる","japanese":"開けられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This door can be opened by anyone.","jp":"このドアは誰でも開けられます。"}},{"english":"close","reading":"しめられる","japanese":"閉められる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you close the window?","jp":"窓を閉められますか？"}},{"english":"go out","reading":"でられる","japanese":"出られる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I wonder if I can leave the house early.","jp":"早く家を出られないかな。"}},{"english":"ride","reading":"のれる","japanese":"乗れる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"You can ride this bus to the station.","jp":"このバスなら駅まで乗れます。"}},{"english":"get off","reading":"おりられる","japanese":"降りられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you get off at the next station?","jp":"次の駅で降りられますか？"}},{"english":"wear","reading":"きられる","japanese":"着られる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can you still wear these clothes?","jp":"この服はまだ着られますか？"}},{"english":"take off","reading":"ぬげる","japanese":"脱げる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"My shoes became easier to take off.","jp":"靴が脱げやすくなった。"}},{"english":"wash","reading":"あらえる","japanese":"洗える","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This shirt can be washed in a washing machine.","jp":"このシャツは洗濯機で洗えます。"}},{"english":"borrow","reading":"かりられる","japanese":"借りられる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Books can be borrowed from the library.","jp":"図書館から本を借りられます。"}},{"english":"return","reading":"かえせる","japanese":"返せる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can return the money by tomorrow morning.","jp":"明日の朝までにお金を返せます。"}},{"english":"explain","reading":"せつめいできる","japanese":"説明できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"This phenomenon can be explained scientifically.","jp":"この現象は科学的に説明できます。"}},{"english":"support","reading":"おうえんできる","japanese":"応援できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can support the team.","jp":"チームを応援できます。"}},{"english":"cooperate","reading":"きょうりょくできる","japanese":"協力できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I will gladly cooperate.","jp":"喜んで協力します。"}},{"english":"participate","reading":"さんかできる","japanese":"参加できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can participate in the meeting.","jp":"会議に参加できます。"}},{"english":"attend","reading":"しゅっせきできる","japanese":"出席できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can attend tomorrow''s party.","jp":"明日のパーティーには出席できます。"}},{"english":"depart","reading":"しゅっぱつできる","japanese":"出発できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"We can depart on time.","jp":"時間通りに出発できます。"}},{"english":"arrive","reading":"とうちゃくできる","japanese":"到着できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"We can arrive earlier than scheduled.","jp":"予定より早く到着できます。"}},{"english":"reserve","reading":"よやくできる","japanese":"予約できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can I reserve a table at the restaurant?","jp":"レストランを予約できますか？"}},{"english":"order","reading":"ちゅうもんできる","japanese":"注文できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"You can order lunch here.","jp":"ここで昼食を注文できます。"}},{"english":"prepare","reading":"じゅんびできる","japanese":"準備できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"The preparations for tomorrow''s meeting are complete.","jp":"明日の会議の準備ができました。"}},{"english":"guide","reading":"あんないできる","japanese":"案内できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can guide you around the city.","jp":"街を案内できます。"}},{"english":"invite","reading":"しょうたいできる","japanese":"招待できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can invite friends to the party.","jp":"友達をパーティーに招待できます。"}},{"english":"introduce","reading":"しょうかいできる","japanese":"紹介できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can introduce him to my friends.","jp":"彼を私の友達に紹介できます。"}},{"english":"consult","reading":"そうだんできる","japanese":"相談できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"Can I consult someone?","jp":"誰かに相談できますか？"}},{"english":"contact","reading":"れんらくできる","japanese":"連絡できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can contact you by tomorrow morning.","jp":"明日の朝までに連絡できます。"}},{"english":"phone","reading":"でんわできる","japanese":"電話できる","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"verb","exampleSentence":{"en":"I can call later.","jp":"後で電話できます。"}},{"english":"humidifier","reading":"かしつき","japanese":"加湿器","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I use a humidifier because it''s dry.","jp":"乾燥するので加湿器を使っています。"}},{"english":"dehumidifier","reading":"じょしつき","japanese":"除湿機","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"A dehumidifier is useful during the rainy season.","jp":"梅雨時期に除湿機が役立ちます。"}},{"english":"air purifier","reading":"くうきせいじょうき","japanese":"空気清浄機","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I leave the air purifier on all the time.","jp":"空気清浄機をつけっぱなしにしています。"}},{"english":"fabric softener","reading":"じゅうなんざい","japanese":"柔軟剤","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"This fabric softener has a nice scent.","jp":"この柔軟剤は良い香りがします。"}},{"english":"deodorizer","reading":"しょうしゅうざい","japanese":"消臭剤","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I placed a deodorizer to remove the room''s smell.","jp":"部屋の臭いを消すために消臭剤を置きました。"}},{"english":"air freshener","reading":"ほうこうざい","japanese":"芳香剤","jlpt_level":"N4","partOfSpeech":"noun","exampleSentence":{"en":"I put an air freshener in the restroom.","jp":"トイレに芳香剤を置きました。"}}]'::jsonb where id = '71b8eafe-1c6b-4c12-a57f-f13d6d00a08c';

-- Word counts in the descriptions — "(405 words)" and a leading "50 essential …"
update starter_packs
